      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a good start, very clear. but to be honest, if i just put that in the library, the score is going to be pretty low because it's quite brief. for the undergrads to really grasp the implications, we need much more depth. \n\ncould you expand on this? i want you to go into the wave-particle duality aspect, the mathematical derivation (even if just conceptual), and maybe some real-world implications for why this matters in quantum chemistry or atomic stability. \n\nagain, i really need the actual substance to be there so it's useful. don't just loop the same sentences or use big words for the sake of it, but please make it much more substantial and comprehensive than that first one.",
      "source": "evaluator"
